          "choice": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A solar eclipse occurs when the moon passes between the Earth and the Sun, blocking all or part of the Sun's light. This alignment causes the moon to cast a shadow on the Earth, which can be observed in specific areas. There are different types of solar eclipses: total, partial, and annular, depending on the alignment and distances involved. During a total eclipse, the day briefly becomes night in the path of totality, where the moon completely covers the Sun."
            }
